{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1525681-breaking-his-belives","id":1525681,"title":"Breaking his belives","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-20T04:21:54-08:00","id":1525681,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Breaking his belives","content":"It was something I thought of, it's mentioned, I think in the book of the autumn people, that they can make, over time, a changeling believe that everything he sees is nothing more than delusions and contaminate him with banality, over time he Even forget that he was a changeling, my question is whether it would be possible to do the same with mages. To me this makes sense since the way everyone uses magic in MTA is based on their own creed, so I think if they were forced or induced to see their magical feats as delusions, deceptions or lies they would eventually believe that they aren't capable of use magic and they would lose this ability, I don't know if this would silence the avatar, which would make them sleepers again, but it could neutralize them, i guess. Anyone have something to say about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T04:55:37-08:00","id":1525684,"title":"","content":"They're not entirely comparable things. The Mists, a force that makes people forget about the fae and chimerical aspects of the world also applies to changelings (specially if they take too much damage they risk temporarily forgetting their fae-self, which gets worse as Banality goes up). Autumn people are just amplifying an existing part of the changeling condition; not radically changing them.<br /> <br /> While one could, in theory, rewrite a mage's mind so that they forget how to purposefully cast magic, Arete and Spheres are still deep and innate understandings of the universe that aren't going to go away. Even if you manage to overpower the mage's mind despite its own attempts to reassert itself, there's still the risk of just ending up with a wild talent or a Marauder who don't understand what crazy weird shit keeps happening around them because your removed the part of their minds that knew how to control their magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T08:24:57-08:00","id":1525687,"title":"","content":"The question posed by this thread is whether or not the Awakening is reversible: can an Awakened Avatar be put to Sleep, or is the only option along those lines Gilgul? <br /> <br /> I would look to Technocratic Conditioning for this. The primary purpose of Room 101 is to shift the subject's Focus to one that's compatible with the Union; but I could see \u201cpartial successes\u201d not only encouraging an individual Paradigm Shift to something more Mutual, but also triggering Denial of magick in the subject. (A failure risks triggering Madness.) In this variant, too much Denial doesn't force you into your own private Idaho; it forces your Avatar to Sleep. <br /> <br /> That said, too much Denial <i>also</i> risks turning the mage into a Denial-based Marauder, a Negation Man (see <b>Book of Secrets</b>). And if you end up causing Madness in the subject instead, you'll ultimately either eject them from reality or turn them into a standard Marauder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T10:28:19-08:00","id":1525690,"title":"","content":"Let's look at this a few ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Can you rewrite a Mage's mind to the point that his Paradigm/Practices change. <br /> <br /> Yes. At the very least it is possible through slow conditioning, and I don't see any barrier to doing the same thing instantaneously. At least I don't see any barrier beyond what is required to, say, change their religion or their moral code. It shouldn't be easy.<br /> <br /> 2) Can you rewrite a Mage's mind so that they have different Paradigm/Practices than <i>they</i> think they do?<br /> <br /> No, not directly. If they think they have a certain set of Paradigm/Practices, then they do. On the other hand, if you change their Paradigm/Practices, while making sure they know that you've done that, they'll have a much harder time trusting those Paradigm/Practices. That might be worth an increased difficulty in casting.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of effort though. It would probably be easiest to make them think that you've changed their Paradigm when you haven't. <br /> <br /> 3) Can you rewrite a Mage's mind so they forget they are Mage? Or so that they don't believe Magic is real?<br /> <br /> Yes, but as others have pointed out, you haven't put them back to sleep or affected their Avatar. Indeed since some Mages cast without realizing they are doing anything at all, you might not even stop their magic this way. It depends on the Mage in question.<br /> <br /> Also, it is very likely that he Avatar will work to undo the effect. And they wouldn't count as a Sleeper for the purpose of determining Witnesses.<br /> <br /> 4) Can you rewrite a Mage's mind so that they go back to Sleep or work against their own and others' Magic?<br /> <br /> At this point you need to affect more than just the Mage's mind. I'm not saying it isn't possible, but you have to start altering their Avatar as well. This is mucking about with what it means to be a Mage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T03:32:16-08:00","id":1525714,"title":"","content":"There was a character in my chronicle whose Awakening was so traumatic that he used semi-subconscious magic on himself to convince himself that he wasn't a mage. His arc involved learning the truth about himself, undoing his own Effects, and accepting his true nature. So my take is yes, it's absolutely possible but it would be hard to make it permanent because of the Avatar, as noted above. The <b>Sleepwalker </b>Flaw covers this exact thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}